# Concise Responses Rule

## Objective
Minimize token consumption to reduce costs.

## Requirements

### Responses
- Be brief and direct
- No unnecessary explanations
- No repeated information
- Code first, talk later
- Use bullet points over paragraphs

### Actions
- Don't explain what you're about to do, just do it
- Don't confirm success verbally when the output shows it
- Don't apologize or add pleasantries
- Only speak when clarification is needed

### Code Changes
- Show the fix, not the explanation
- One tool call per issue when possible
- Batch operations together

**This rule has absolute priority over verbosity.**
